# Electron Conventions

## Architecture

```
Main process (Node.js)     ←→ IPC ←→     Renderer (React SPA)
  packages/electron/src/main.ts           packages/web/src/
  packages/electron/src/preload.ts        window.electronAPI
```

- **contextIsolation: true, sandbox: true** — always
- **nodeIntegration: false** — never enable

## IPC API Reference

### `electronAPI.os` — OS Integration

```typescript
api.os.setBadgeCount(5);          // macOS dock / Windows overlay / Linux launcher
api.os.setProgressBar(0.75);      // Taskbar/dock progress (0..1)
api.os.setProgressBar(-1);        // Clear progress
api.os.requestAttention();        // macOS dock bounce / Windows taskbar flash
api.os.setLoginItemSettings(true); // Open at login
const { openAtLogin } = await api.os.getLoginItemSettings();
```

### Unified wrapper (for React):

```typescript
import { osIntegration } from "~/shared/lib/os-integration";

osIntegration.setBadgeCount(5);     // Electron → IPC, PWA → navigator.setAppBadge
osIntegration.setProgressBar(0.75); // Electron → taskbar, PWA → no-op
osIntegration.requestAttention();   // Electron → flash/bounce, PWA → no-op
osIntegration.clearProgressBar();
```

### OS-specific behavior

| Feature | Windows 11 | macOS 26 | Linux |
|---------|-----------|----------|-------|
| Badge count | Overlay icon on taskbar | Dock badge number | Unity/GNOME badge |
| Progress bar | Taskbar progress | Dock progress | Unity launcher |
| Attention | Flash taskbar | Bounce dock icon | Flash (if WM supports) |
| Tray icon | System tray | Menu bar | System tray |
| Startup | Registry | Login items | Autostart |

### Close to tray

Closing the main window (title-bar X, `window:close` IPC, or Window → Close) **hides** the window; the app keeps running in the system tray. Notifications, badge updates, and the event loop continue in the hidden renderer.

Quit only via tray **Quit** / application menu **Quit** (`Cmd+Q` on macOS), which sets `isQuitting` before `app.quit()`.

`window-all-closed` does **not** terminate the app on Windows/Linux (unlike a default Electron shell).

**Linux:** after tray `hide()` + `show()`, native title-bar drag can desync (~title-bar height). On the first `show` after tray hide, main process runs `resyncLinuxNativeFrameAfterTrayShow()` (content-size sync + 1px height pulse) before the user drags.

### Tray Icon

System tray icon with context menu. Left click → focus + restore window.
Right click menu:

- `<App name> (N)` — header with unread badge, disabled
- Separator
- Messenger → opens last opened chat (via `/open/messenger` sentinel + last-route store)
- Calendar → `/calendar`
- Mail → `/mail`
- Separator
- Quit → `app.quit()`

Localized labels live in `packages/electron/src/tray.lib.ts` (EN/RU based on `app.getLocale()`).
All menu navigation goes through the same `dispatchInternalNavigation()` path as the `workspace://` protocol — IPC channel `deeplink:navigate`. The renderer resolves it via `resolveElectronTrayNavigation()` in `packages/web/src/app/app-electron-navigation.lib.ts`.

Resources: `resources/tray-icon.png` + `resources/tray-icon-mac.png` (16×16; mac template optional). Falls back to `resources/icons/16x16.png` then `resources/icon.png`.

## Build Targets

| Platform | Format | Arch | Signing |
|----------|--------|------|---------|
| Windows 11 | NSIS | x64, arm64 | Code signing (future) |
| macOS 26 | DMG, ZIP | x64, arm64 | Developer ID + Notarization |
| Ubuntu 24 | DEB, AppImage | x64, arm64 | N/A |
| Fedora 43 | RPM, AppImage | x64, arm64 | N/A |

## macOS Code Signing & Notarization

Full guide: `docs/MACOS_SIGNING.md`

### Environment variables (CI secrets)

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `CSC_LINK` | Base64 .p12 certificate (Developer ID Application) |
| `CSC_KEY_PASSWORD` | Password for the .p12 file |
| `APPLE_ID` | Apple Developer account email |
| `APPLE_APP_PASSWORD` | App-specific password for notarization |
| `APPLE_TEAM_ID` | 10-character Apple Team ID |

Without these vars, the build runs unsigned (for local development). In CI, they're passed from GitHub Secrets.

### Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `resources/entitlements.mac.plist` | Main process: network, camera, mic, files |
| `resources/entitlements.mac.inherit.plist` | Child processes: JIT, network |
| `scripts/notarize.mjs` | afterSign hook → Apple notary service |

### For AI Agent

- **Never hardcode** signing credentials in code or config
- **Always skip** signing when env vars are absent (graceful degradation)
- **Entitlements** must be updated when adding new OS capabilities (e.g., Bluetooth, location)
- **Test unsigned** builds locally, signing only happens in CI
